Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:56:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 101/260] [ae-patch] Slide the session rail out only while the
 workspace panel slides open, so a session switch does not squeeze the chat

Since the v0.18 sync the workspace panel animates only when its header
toggle, a link or a tab opens or closes it (setRightPanelOpenAnimated,
data-animate-visibility); a session restore snaps it. With "Open the
session rail in every session" off, a switch to a session whose panel was
saved open snapped the panel to full width while the rail slid out over
300 ms, so both showed and the chat dropped from 437 px to 181 px for
about 280 ms.

The shell now passes its rightPanelVisibilityAnimating flag as
workspace.animating, and the rail slides out in its row only when it made
way for a panel that is sliding open. A snapped panel makes it leave at
once, as a push panel already does.
